KIARA in the 25 Mpc EAGLE volume at 8x lower resolution than EAGLE
(L0025N0188: 188^3 dark matter particles, the same number of gas particles
generated at start-up; gas particle mass 1.45e7 Msun).

This is close to the resolution at which KIARA is calibrated (25 Mpc/h,
256^3), so kiara_25.yml uses the calibrated subgrid parameters unchanged.
It is meant to be kept up to date with the current calibration. Only the
cosmology (EAGLE / Planck 2013, to match the ICs), the IC options and the
file names differ from the calibration runs.

The code should be configured with

  --with-subgrid=KIARA --with-hydro=magma2 --with-kernel=wendland-C2

(plus any compiler, library or MPI options for your system; no external
Grackle library is needed, the KIARA cooling uses a built-in crackle).

run.sh fetches the ICs (with ../../EAGLE_ICs/EAGLE_25_low_res/getIC.sh) and
the Cloudy cooling table, then runs SWIFT with --cosmology --kiara. The chem5
tables are read from ../chem5.

MD5 hash of the ICs:
62e7ec93a1b0b4c57ff0c63ad0da2028  EAGLE_L0025N0188_ICs.hdf5
